### Test Error Handling

### 1. Test Health Check (Should return success with new format)
GET http://localhost:3000/health

###

### 2. Test Get Users (Empty or with data)
GET http://localhost:3000/users

###

### 3. Test Create User (Success)
POST http://localhost:3000/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com"
}

###

### 4. Test Create Duplicate Email (Should return CONFLICT error)
POST http://localhost:3000/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com"
}

###

### 5. Test Get User by ID (Not Found Error)
GET http://localhost:3000/users/999

###

### 6. Test Get User by ID (Success)
GET http://localhost:3000/users/1

###

### 7. Test Update User (Success)
PUT http://localhost:3000/users/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Updated",
  "email": "john.updated@example.com"
}

###

### 8. Test Update User (Not Found)
PUT http://localhost:3000/users/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test",
  "email": "test@example.com"
}

###

### 9. Test Delete User (Success)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/users/1

###

### 10. Test Delete User (Not Found)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/users/999

###

### 11. Test Invalid Route (404 Error)
GET http://localhost:3000/invalid-route

###

